From: j7
Subject: j7: default the GPU PLL to its verified 900 MHz

The last boot cmdline carried j7gpu=7 but not j7gpuclk, so the G3D PLL stayed at the 343 MHz
the bootloader leaves and the 900 MHz step the 0374 boot verified was never reached.  The
GPU is the same Mali-T830 running Mesa's Panfrost driver that the herolte port uses on its
T880, so its clock is the whole of the GPU-side speed available without writing a Metal
driver, and there is no reason to make every boot repeat an argument for it.

Default j7gpuclk to 900 MHz: the value is range-checked, the PLL is written at the P and S
the bootloader chose (P 13, S 1 makes the output M MHz, so M=900 is an 1800 MHz VCO), and
the register is read back and decoded into the log.  j7gpuclk=0 keeps the bootloader rate.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -795,9 +795,12 @@
 				 * j7gpuclk=<kHz> reprograms PLL_CON0 - M 343 -> 900 at the same P 13, S 1,
 				 * which is 1800 MHz in the VCO and 900 out. The top byte of CON0 is kept
 				 * because what those bits mean is not documented. */
-				int want = 0;
-				if (PE_parse_boot_argn("j7gpuclk", &want, sizeof(want)) && want >= 200 &&
-				    want <= 1000 && (uint32_t)want != pll) {
+				/* 900 MHz is the rate the 0374 boot read back and the only GPU step
+				 * measured on this phone; default to it so no boot argument is needed.
+				 * j7gpuclk=0 keeps whatever the bootloader left. */
+				int want = 900;
+				PE_parse_boot_argn("j7gpuclk", &want, sizeof(want));
+				if (want >= 200 && want <= 1000 && (uint32_t)want != pll) {
 					uint32_t gp_p = (gp != 0) ? gp : 13u;
 					uint32_t gp_s = gs;
 					/* Fout = 26 MHz * M / (P << S), so M = Fout * (P << S) / 26 MHz.
